# UI: names, not IDs

In user-facing copy (screens, toasts, AI messages, map markers, labels):

- **Never** show raw identifiers: UUIDs, numeric user ids, opaque tokens, truncated id prefixes.
- **Always** show human names/titles: work order title, site name, user display name / email, equipment name, map/item titles.
- If a name is missing, use a **generic label** (`Заявка`, `Инженер`, `Пользователь`, `Площадка`) — not the id.
- IDs stay in APIs, logs, deep links, and internal state; they must not leak into visible text.

## Examples

```text
❌ Заявка: 412138a9-249b-4790-a320-5e8cc9cf84d4 · Инженер: 383177205334671363
✅ Заявка: Утечка · Инженер: Иван Петров

❌ marker label = userId.take(8)
✅ marker label = displayName ?: "Инженер"
```

Existing helpers: `formatAssigneeLabel`, `resolvePprLabels` — follow the same pattern for new UI.
